{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc | sed -n '1,220p' && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc | sed -n '220,470p' && nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/http.cljc | sed -n '275,385p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.star.lease\n     2\t  \"The dao.lease compositions of dao.star Mode 1 (docs/design/dao.star.md,\n     3\t   Liveness): the stream-reading helper, the holder agent a driver threads per\n     4\t   lease, and the two grantor-side wrappers (exchange lease, lineage lease)\n     5\t   that author grants and drive the judge.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Nothing here reads a clock.  Time is the `:dao.lease/reading` data drained\n     8\t   from a tick stream the composition feeds, so every lapse is driven by\n     9\t   appending a tick.\"\n    10\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    11\t            [dao.lease :as lease]\n    12\t            [dao.star.facts :as facts]\n    13\t            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t(defn- ok?\n    17\t  [r]\n    18\t  (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t(defn oldest-cursor\n    22\t  [handle]\n    23\t  (let [r (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest)]\n    24\t    (when-not (ok? r)\n    25\t      (throw (ex-info \"cannot mint a cursor\" {:outcome r})))\n    26\t    (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn drain\n    30\t  \"Read `handle` from `cursor` to `blocked`, never waiting.  Answers\n    31\t   `{:cursor c :values [v...] :gap? bool :end? bool}`: a `gap` is noted and\n    32\t   reading continues from its recovery cursor, as the contract has it.\"\n    33\t  [handle cursor]\n    34\t  (loop [c cursor values [] gap? false]\n    35\t    (let [r (stream/next handle c)]\n    36\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n    37\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj values (:dao.stream/value r)) gap?)\n    38\t        :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) values true)\n    39\t        :dao.stream/end {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? true}\n    40\t        {:cursor c :values values :gap? gap? :end? false}))))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    44\t;; Holder agent: one lease, held by a driver's control flow\n    45\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn make-agent\n    48\t  \"A holder over `lease/make-holder` plus the cursors its control flow drains.\n    49\t   `config` is `make-holder`'s, less the cursors (minted here at the oldest\n    50\t   anchor, so a grant already on the medium is observed).  `:envelope` is merged\n    51\t   into every fact the agent appends (the lineage lease stamps\n    52\t   `:dao.star/lineage` here, which is what the judge's resolver attributes by).\n    53\t   Answers an atom holding the agent state.\"\n    54\t  [{:keys [tick fact writer envelope] :as config}]\n    55\t  (let [wired (lease/make-holder\n    56\t                (assoc config\n    57\t                       :tick {:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}\n    58\t                       :fact {:handle (:handle fact)\n    59\t                              :cursor (oldest-cursor (:handle fact))\n    60\t                              :source (:source fact)\n    61\t                              :medium (:medium fact)}\n    62\t                       :writer writer))]\n    63\t    (atom {:holder (:holder wired)\n    64\t           :tick (:tick wired)\n    65\t           :fact (:fact wired)\n    66\t           :writer (:writer wired)\n    67\t           :envelope (or envelope {})\n    68\t           :reading nil\n    69\t           :lapsed? false\n    70\t           :gapped? false\n    71\t           :release nil})))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t(defn- lease-id\n    75\t  [a]\n    76\t  (get-in a [:holder :grant :dao.lease/lease]))\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\t(defn- usable-reading?\n    80\t  \"True for a reading the holder can observe with: a well-shaped duration in\n    81\t   the holder's unit table and within its per-unit bound (what `observe-grant`\n    82\t   itself requires).\"\n    83\t  [holder reading]\n    84\t  (and (lease/duration? reading)\n    85\t       (let [k (first (keys reading))\n    86\t             m (get (:units holder) k)]\n    87\t         (and (some? m)\n    88\t              (<= (get reading k) (quot lease/magnitude-limit m))))))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn step!\n    92\t  \"One control-flow pass of the holder: drain its own tick cursor for the\n    93\t   newest reading, then observe its grant (before anything else) and any\n    94\t   `:lapsed` record for its lease.  The fact cursor advances only once a usable\n    95\t   reading exists: facts published before it stay unread on the medium, in\n    96\t   order, until a reading can observe them, so a grant is never skipped and a\n    97\t   lapse that follows it is never read ahead of it.  A `gap` on either cursor\n    98\t   marks the agent `:gapped?`: it renews nothing from then on.  Answers the new\n    99\t   state.\"\n   100\t  [agent]\n   101\t  (swap!\n   102\t    agent\n   103\t    (fn [a]\n   104\t      (let [t (drain (get-in a [:tick :handle]) (get-in a [:tick :cursor]))\n   105\t            reading (or (some-> (filter #(= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event %))\n   106\t                                        (:values t))\n   107\t                                last\n   108\t                                :dao.lease/reading)\n   109\t                        (:reading a))\n   110\t            a (-> a\n   111\t                  (assoc :reading reading)\n   112\t                  (assoc-in [:tick :cursor] (:cursor t))\n   113\t                  (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? t))))]\n   114\t        (if-not (usable-reading? (:holder a) reading)\n   115\t          a\n   116\t          (let [f (drain (get-in a [:fact :handle]) (get-in a [:fact :cursor]))\n   117\t                a (-> a\n   118\t                      (assoc-in [:fact :cursor] (:cursor f))\n   119\t                      (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? f))))]\n   120\t            (reduce\n   121\t              (fn [a v]\n   122\t                (cond\n   123\t                  (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   124\t                  (update a :holder lease/observe-grant (get-in a [:fact :source]) v reading)\n   125\t\n   126\t                  (and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status v))\n   127\t                       (some? (lease-id a))\n   128\t                       (= (lease-id a) (:dao.lease/lease v)))\n   129\t                  (assoc a :lapsed? true)\n   130\t\n   131\t                  :else a))\n   132\t              a\n   133\t              (:values f))))))))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn gapped?\n   137\t  \"True once any cursor the agent reads answered `gap`.\"\n   138\t  [agent]\n   139\t  (boolean (:gapped? @agent)))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn release-pending?\n   143\t  \"True while a release fact is staged and not yet appended with `ok`.\"\n   144\t  [agent]\n   145\t  (some? (:release @agent)))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(defn holding?\n   149\t  \"May the control flow act: a grant observed, not stopped, not at its bound,\n   150\t   not lapsed, and no gap seen.\"\n   151\t  [agent]\n   152\t  (let [a @agent]\n   153\t    (boolean (and (not (:lapsed? a))\n   154\t                  (not (:gapped? a))\n   155\t                  (some? (:reading a))\n   156\t                  (lease/holding? (:holder a) (:reading a))))))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t(defn granted?\n   160\t  [agent]\n   161\t  (some? (get-in @agent [:holder :grant])))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn past-bound?\n   165\t  \"True once the agent has left the lease for good: it lapsed, was released,\n   166\t   or reached its bound.  A gap is not that: the agent renews nothing after one\n   167\t   but the lease is not known to be over.\"\n   168\t  [agent]\n   169\t  (let [a @agent]\n   170\t    (boolean (or (:lapsed? a)\n   171\t                 (get-in a [:holder :released?])\n   172\t                 (get-in a [:holder :bound-reached?])\n   173\t                 (and (some? (:reading a)) (some? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   174\t                      (lease/at-bound? (:holder a) (:reading a)))))))\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\t(defn- append-renewal!\n   178\t  [agent]\n   179\t  (let [a @agent\n   180\t        fact (merge (lease/renewal (lease-id a)) (:envelope a))\n   181\t        outcome (stream/append! (get-in a [:writer :handle]) fact)]\n   182\t    (swap! agent update :holder lease/observe-renewal (:reading a) outcome)\n   183\t    outcome))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn renew-if-due!\n   187\t  \"Renew when the holder's interval has been reached.  Answers true when a\n   188\t   renewal was appended.\"\n   189\t  [agent]\n   190\t  (let [a @agent]\n   191\t    (boolean\n   192\t      (when (and (holding? agent) (lease/due-to-renew? (:holder a) (:reading a)))\n   193\t        (append-renewal! agent)\n   194\t        true))))\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\t(defn renew!\n   198\t  \"Renew now, on a consumed input.  A holder that is not holding renews\n   199\t   nothing.\"\n   200\t  [agent]\n   201\t  (boolean (when (holding? agent) (append-renewal! agent) true)))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn release!\n   205\t  \"Release on halt.  The release fact is kept until its append answers ok, so a\n   206\t   failed append retries the same fact.\"\n   207\t  [agent]\n   208\t  (let [a @agent]\n   209\t    (when (and (granted? agent) (not (get-in a [:holder :released?])))\n   210\t      (let [{:keys [holder release]} (lease/stop (:holder a))]\n   211\t        (swap! agent assoc :holder holder :release (merge release (:envelope a)))))\n   212\t    (when-let [fact (:release @agent)]\n   213\t      (when (ok? (stream/append! (get-in @agent [:writer :handle]) fact))\n   214\t        (swap! agent assoc :release nil :released-sent? true)))\n   215\t    agent))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   219\t;; Grantor side: exchange lease\n   220\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   220\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   221\t\n   222\t(def resolver-bindings #{:per-author-media :envelope-key})\n   223\t\n   224\t(def exchange-source :egress)\n   225\t(def lineage-source :session-facts)\n   226\t(def exchange-lease-source :exchange-lease)\n   227\t(def lineage-lease-source :lineage-lease)\n   228\t(def exchange-grantor :boundary-judge)\n   229\t(def lineage-grantor :lineage-judge)\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn resolver\n   233\t  \"The one attribution the star compositions share.  Per-author media: the\n   234\t   source names the author.  Envelope key: the session-facts medium is written\n   235\t   only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage`, and that stamp\n   236\t   names the author.  A fact's own claim of authorship is never consulted.\"\n   237\t  [source fact]\n   238\t  (if (= lineage-source source)\n   239\t    (when-let [s (:dao.star/lineage fact)] {:dao.star/lineage s})\n   240\t    (case source\n   241\t      :egress :egress\n   242\t      :exchange-lease exchange-grantor\n   243\t      :lineage-lease lineage-grantor\n   244\t      nil)))\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\t(defn medium-declaration\n   248\t  [capacity attribution]\n   249\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity capacity\n   250\t   :value-domain :portable-values :attribution attribution})\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t(defn facts-declaration\n   254\t  \"The declaration of the session-facts medium: complete history, no capacity.\"\n   255\t  []\n   256\t  {:retention :complete :value-domain :portable-values})\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn check-facts-declaration!\n   260\t  \"Assembly check, on the declaration and not the handle: the session-facts\n   261\t   medium must be declared `:retention :complete`.  Answers the declaration.\"\n   262\t  [decl]\n   263\t  (when-not (and (map? decl) (= :complete (:retention decl)) (not (contains? decl :capacity)))\n   264\t    (throw (ex-info \"the session-facts medium must be declared :retention :complete\"\n   265\t                    {:refused :session-facts :declaration decl})))\n   266\t  decl)\n   267\t\n   268\t\n   269\t(defn make-exchange-lease\n   270\t  \"The grantor half of the exchange lease, composed inside the peer holding the\n   271\t   HTTP boundary.  Config:\n   272\t     :ingress :egress :lease-medium  the three media (handles)\n   273\t     :tick                           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   274\t     :open-exchanges :close-exchange the boundary's inventory and reclaim\n   275\t     :units :duration :cadence :tolerance\n   276\t     :subscription-max               required duration: the `:dao.lease/max` every\n   277\t                                     subscription exchange's grant carries, the\n   278\t                                     dead-peer bound on a host that reports\n   279\t                                     neither close nor failed write\n   280\t     :capacity                       declared capacity of the egress medium\n   281\t   The judge reads the egress medium for the responders' renewals and writes\n   282\t   grants and `:lapsed` to the lease medium.  Policy ends the lease of an\n   283\t   exchange the inventory no longer holds (peer close, gap reconciliation), and\n   284\t   reclaim is the boundary's idempotent `close-exchange`, reporting success when\n   285\t   the exchange is not open afterwards.\"\n   286\t  [{:keys [ingress egress lease-medium tick open-exchanges close-exchange\n   287\t           units duration cadence tolerance capacity subscription-max]}]\n   288\t  (when-not (lease/duration? subscription-max)\n   289\t    (throw (ex-info \"a subscription exchange needs a :dao.lease/max (:subscription-max, a duration)\"\n   290\t                    {:refused :subscription-cap :subscription-max subscription-max})))\n   291\t  (let [reclaim (fn [subject]\n   292\t                  (let [id (:http/exchange subject)]\n   293\t                    (close-exchange id)\n   294\t                    (not (contains? (open-exchanges) id))))\n   295\t        policy (fn [entry _now]\n   296\t                 (not (contains? (open-exchanges)\n   297\t                                 (:http/exchange (:subject entry)))))\n   298\t        made (lease/make-judge\n   299\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   300\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   301\t                :reclaim reclaim :policy policy\n   302\t                :writer lease-medium :self exchange-grantor\n   303\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   304\t                :media [{:handle egress :cursor (oldest-cursor egress)\n   305\t                         :source exchange-source\n   306\t                         :medium (medium-declaration capacity :per-author-media)}]})]\n   307\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   308\t           :ingress ingress :ingress-cursor (oldest-cursor ingress)\n   309\t           :open-exchanges open-exchanges\n   310\t           :duration duration :subscription-max subscription-max :leased #{}})))\n   311\t\n   312\t\n   313\t(defn- grant-exchange\n   314\t  \"Grant exchange `id` unsolicited.  A subscription (`/s/…`), and any exchange\n   315\t   whose kind is unknown (gap reconciliation), carries the tenure cap.\"\n   316\t  [x id subscription?]\n   317\t  (swap! x (fn [s]\n   318\t             (-> s\n   319\t                 (update :judge lease/author-grant\n   320\t                         (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) {:http/exchange id}\n   321\t                                      :egress (:duration s)\n   322\t                                      (when subscription?\n   323\t                                        {:dao.lease/max (:subscription-max s)})))\n   324\t                 (update :leased conj id))))\n   325\t  x)\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn exchange-lease-step!\n   329\t  \"One pass: observe the ingress for each `:http/request` and grant its\n   330\t   exchange unsolicited; on an ingress gap reconcile against the inventory (an\n   331\t   open exchange without a lease is granted afresh; a leased exchange absent\n   332\t   from the inventory is ended by the judge's policy with cause `:policy`);\n   333\t   then one judge pass.  Answers the atom.\"\n   334\t  [x]\n   335\t  (let [s @x\n   336\t        r (drain (:ingress s) (:ingress-cursor s))\n   337\t        open ((:open-exchanges s))]\n   338\t    (swap! x assoc :ingress-cursor (:cursor r))\n   339\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   340\t            :when (= :http/request (:http/event v))\n   341\t            :let [id (:http/exchange v)]\n   342\t            :when (and (contains? open id) (not (contains? (:leased @x) id)))]\n   343\t      (grant-exchange x id (str/starts-with? (str (:http/path v)) \"/s/\")))\n   344\t    (when (:gap? r)\n   345\t      (doseq [id open :when (not (contains? (:leased @x) id))]\n   346\t        (grant-exchange x id true)))\n   347\t    ;; Forget what is closed: its lease is the judge's to end.\n   348\t    (swap! x update :leased #(into #{} (filter open) %))\n   349\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   350\t    x))\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   354\t;; Grantor side: lineage lease\n   355\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   356\t\n   357\t(defn make-lineage-lease\n   358\t  \"The grantor half of the lineage lease.  Config:\n   359\t     :facts          the session-facts medium (handle)\n   360\t     :lease-medium   where grants and `:lapsed` are written (handle)\n   361\t     :tick           the judge's tick stream (handle)\n   362\t     :retire!        (fn [lineage]) retiring the parked record\n   363\t     :units :duration :max :cadence :tolerance\n   364\t     :facts-declaration  the facts medium's declaration, `:retention :complete`\n   365\t   Each root fact read grants unsolicited, subject and holder\n   366\t   `{:dao.star/lineage S}`.  The judge reads the same medium for the drivers'\n   367\t   renewals and releases, attributed by the `:dao.star/lineage` envelope key.\"\n   368\t  [{:keys [lease-medium tick retire! units duration cadence tolerance]\n   369\t    cap :max session-facts :facts declaration :facts-declaration}]\n   370\t  (check-facts-declaration! declaration)\n   371\t  (let [made (lease/make-judge\n   372\t               {:units units :cadence cadence :tolerance tolerance\n   373\t                :resolver resolver :resolver-bindings resolver-bindings\n   374\t                :reclaim (fn [subject]\n   375\t                           (retire! (:dao.star/lineage subject))\n   376\t                           true)\n   377\t                :writer lease-medium :self lineage-grantor\n   378\t                :ticks [{:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}]\n   379\t                :media [{:handle session-facts :cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   380\t                         :source lineage-source\n   381\t                         :medium (assoc declaration :attribution :envelope-key)}]})]\n   382\t    (atom {:judge (:judge made) :step (:step made)\n   383\t           :facts session-facts :facts-cursor (oldest-cursor session-facts)\n   384\t           :duration duration :max cap})))\n   385\t\n   386\t\n   387\t(defn lineage-lease-step!\n   388\t  \"One pass: grant each newly read root, then one judge pass.\"\n   389\t  [x]\n   390\t  (let [s @x\n   391\t        r (drain (:facts s) (:facts-cursor s))]\n   392\t    (swap! x assoc :facts-cursor (:cursor r))\n   393\t    (doseq [v (:values r)\n   394\t            :when (and (map? v) (= :root (facts/fact-kind v)))\n   395\t            :let [subject {:dao.star/lineage (:dao.star/lineage v)}]]\n   396\t      (swap! x update :judge lease/author-grant\n   397\t             (lease/grant (lease/mint-lease-id) subject subject (:duration s)\n   398\t                          (when (:max s) {:dao.lease/max (:max s)}))))\n   399\t    (swap! x (fn [s] (update s :judge (:step s))))\n   400\t    x))\n   275\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   276\t\n   277\t(defn- effect?\n   278\t  [v]\n   279\t  (and (map? v) (contains? v :http/exchange) (keyword? (:http/effect v))))\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\t(defn- chunk-payload?\n   283\t  [x]\n   284\t  (or (string? x) (bytes/bytes? x)))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- perform!\n   288\t  \"Perform one effect for an exchange this boundary holds open.\"\n   289\t  [boundary id entry effect]\n   290\t  (let [socket (:socket entry)\n   291\t        phase (:phase entry)\n   292\t        fail! (fn [] (when-let [e (claim! boundary id)] (close-claimed! boundary id e)))\n   293\t        set-phase! (fn [p]\n   294\t                     (swap! (:state boundary)\n   295\t                            (fn [s]\n   296\t                              (if (contains? (:open s) id)\n   297\t                                (assoc-in s [:open id :phase] p)\n   298\t                                s))))]\n   299\t    (case (:http/effect effect)\n   300\t      :http/head\n   301\t      (if (and (= :new phase) (integer? (:http/status effect)))\n   302\t        (if (seam-ok? (:head! socket) (:http/status effect) (or (:http/headers effect) {}))\n   303\t          (set-phase! :streaming)\n   304\t          (fail!))\n   305\t        (fail!))\n   306\t\n   307\t      :http/chunk\n   308\t      (if (and (= :streaming phase) (chunk-payload? (:http/body effect)))\n   309\t        (when-not (seam-ok? (:write! socket) (:http/body effect))\n   310\t          (fail!))\n   311\t        (fail!))\n   312\t\n   313\t      :http/end\n   314\t      (if (= :streaming phase)\n   315\t        (when-let [e (claim! boundary id)]\n   316\t          (if (seam-ok? (:end! socket))\n   317\t            (finish! boundary id e :http/ended)\n   318\t            (close-claimed! boundary id e)))\n   319\t        (fail!))\n   320\t\n   321\t      ;; An effect kind this interpreter does not know is not its own.\n   322\t      nil)))\n   323\t\n   324\t\n   325\t(defn- stop-listener!\n   326\t  [boundary]\n   327\t  (when-let [f (:on-stop @(:state boundary))]\n   328\t    (try (f) (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn stop!\n   332\t  \"Boundary stop: close every open exchange (each deposits `:http/closed`),\n   333\t   refuse further requests, and stop the listener.  Idempotent.\"\n   334\t  [boundary]\n   335\t  (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :stopped? true)\n   336\t  (close-all! boundary)\n   337\t  (stop-listener! boundary)\n   338\t  boundary)\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(defn on-stop!\n   342\t  \"Register the host listener's stop function, run when the boundary stops or\n   343\t   its egress medium ends.\"\n   344\t  [boundary f]\n   345\t  (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :on-stop f)\n   346\t  boundary)\n   347\t\n   348\t\n   349\t(defn egress-step\n   350\t  \"Perform the effects the egress medium holds, in its order, until it has\n   351\t   none more; never waits.  Answers the boundary.\"\n   352\t  [boundary]\n   353\t  (loop []\n   354\t    (let [s @(:state boundary)]\n   355\t      (when-not (:stopped? s)\n   356\t        (let [r (stream/next (:egress boundary) (:cursor s))\n   357\t              outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   358\t          (condp = outcome\n   359\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   360\t            (do (swap! (:state boundary) assoc :cursor (:dao.stre